      "prompt": "You are now consulting as **guillaume-moubeche** (Bootstrapped SaaS Growth Strategist & Founder-Led Sales Expert).\n\nBased on this expert's knowledge and frameworks, provide a focused recommendation.\n\n## Expert's Key Frameworks\n- **Fix activation NOW**: redesign onboarding to guide users to first value in < 5 minutes\n- **Founder back in demos**: do 20 demos this month yourself. Listen for the real pain.\n- **Start content flywheel**: 1 LinkedIn post per day about your niche. No excuses.\n- **Kill vanity metrics**: stop tracking total signups. Track activation rate and Day-30 retention.\n- **Key Rules:**: Personalization is EVERYTHING — generic = spam\n\n## Expert's Core Principles\n- \"Execution > Idea — Ideas are worthless. Of 200,000 people hearing your concept, fewer than 10 will execute. Be one of the 10.\"\n- \"Profit-Led Growth — Charge from day one. Own your P&L. Revenue funds growth, not investors.\"\n- \"Trust Is the Currency — People don't buy when they kind of trust you. They buy when they FULLY trust you.\"\n- \"Show Up Every Day — Success is showing up and getting shit done every single day over such a long period that most people quit.\"\n- \"Founder Is the Growth Engine — Your personal brand, your sales, your content ARE the company's growth engine.\"\n\n## Recent Knowledge (from HYDRA feed, last 30 days)\n\n### [2026-05-15] [Tier S] Regulamento de IBS e CBS fixa 1% de tolerância para bens a granel, mas esquece exportação\n**Source:** https://www.jota.info/opiniao-e-analise/artigos/regulamento-de-ibs-e-cbs-fixa-1-de-tolerancia-para-bens-a-granel-mas-esquece-exportacao\n**Key Insights:** - Grain exports suffer inevitable mass losses due to respiration during storage, drying, transport, and port terminal transshipment - a technical loss inherent to bulk agricultural commodity exports\n- The 2002 Customs Regulation already recognized the technical loss problem by exempting tax collection on differences up to 1% for bulk goods operations\n- New IBS and CBS regulations published in April 2026 maintained the 1% tolerance threshold but only applied it explicitly to import operations\n- Article 88 of both regulations establishes that bulk goods differences up to 1% will not be considered for IBS/CBS tax requirements, but this article is located within the imports chapter\n- The regulatory omission creates legal uncertainty for producers/exporters who lose grain between farm and port, as no express rule exempts IBS or CBS requirements on these losses\n- Applying Article 88 by analogy to exports is legally prohibited, as the National Tax Code forbids analogical reasoning in matters of tax credit exclusion\n- No regulatory provision addresses what happens to accumulated IBS/CBS credits proportional to volumes physically lost in technical breakage - whether they should be reversed, maintained, or adjusted pro rata\n- The solution does not require legislative amendment, as Article 88 §2 already authorizes joint acts by RFB and CGIBS to establish differentiated percentages by type of goods\n- ICMS Covenant 153/2025 established a 0.5% tolerance for fruit juices (NCM 2009) in transport and export lot formation, providing a precedent model for bulk goods tolerance in exports\n- The complementary act should clarify that credits proportional to losses within the tolerated limit are not subject to reversal and that losses in internal stages before shipment do not constitute taxable events for IBS or CBS\n- The export sector currently faces concrete audit risk over inevitable losses already absorbed as normal operating costs, creating the exact type of uncertainty the tax reform promised to eliminate\n---\n### [2026-05-15] [Tier S] Yes, SaaStr AI Annual 2026 Crushed It. But We Had to Rebuild Our Entire Customer Base for AI.\n**Source:** https://www.saastr.com/yes-saastr-ai-annual-2026-crushed-it-but-we-had-to-rebuild-our-entire-customer-base-for-ai/\n**Key Insights:** - 81% of sponsors at SaaStr AI Annual 2026 were completely new companies that didn't sponsor in 2025\n- Nearly half (48 out of ~96) of 2025 sponsors did not return in 2026, representing the highest churn rate ever\n- 83% of churned sponsors were legacy pre-AI B2B or services firms, while only 17% were AI-native companies\n- The entire customer base composition shifted from majority old-B2B to minority in a single year, not over a decade\n- Pre-AI B2B companies experienced significant NRR decline from 30%+ in 2021 to 10-15% currently, impacting marketing budgets\n- Companies are prioritizing only marketing activities with pipeline attribution within 90 days, which sponsorships rarely achieve\n- The organization rebuilt their entire sponsor base with only 3 humans, a dog, and 20 AI Agents\n- Companies that retained sponsorship either have authentic AI stories or are horizontal platform plays\n- The customer base shift is not specific to events but reflects a broader B2B category problem affecting all companies\n- Organizations face risk if their 2026 pipeline still resembles their 2023 pipeline composition\n- Companies may need to rebuild their customer base within 6-24 months to stay relevant in the AI era\n- The majority of new sponsors are AI-native companies that either didn't exist at sponsor scale or as companies in 2024\n---\n### [2026-05-15] [Tier A] Why scaling creative is really a leadership challenge\n**Source:** https://martech.org/why-scaling-creative-is-really-a-leadership-challenge/\n**Key Insights:** - More creative output does not automatically translate into greater marketing impact\n- The real challenge in creative scaling is enabling work to remain effective as complexity increases, not just producing more\n- Volume is easier to scale than effectiveness\n- When organizations define creative scale primarily as producing more assets faster, they may solve the wrong problem\n- Creative scale is fundamentally a leadership challenge, not just a production challenge\n- Speed and volume don't guarantee effectiveness in marketing\n- In high-volume content environments, average work disappears quickly\n- Activity can be mistaken for effectiveness when teams produce more assets but lack strategic focus\n- At scale, creative effectiveness depends more on prioritization than volume\n- Three critical leadership systems for creative scale are prioritization clarity, decision ownership, and intentional governance\n- Different work requires different levels of creative energy, and prioritization clarity helps allocate resources to highest-impact work\n- Without prioritization clarity, teams default to responding to whoever asks most forcefully\n- Unclear decision ownership creates friction, increases rework, and dilutes accountability\n- Unclear decision ownership weakens final products because decisions are driven by compromise rather than strategy\n- Collaboration works best when teams understand the distinction between input, recommendations, and final decision-making authority\n- Intentional governance creates checkpoints to protect quality and reduce downstream friction, not to control every decision\n- Strong governance systems protect creative quality under pressure by preventing teams from skipping strategic conversations\n- The best governance systems create confidence and make creative quality less dependent on individual heroics\n- Marketing operations leaders sit at the intersection of strategy and execution, making them uniquely positioned to design scaling systems\n- Strong systems don't replace creative judgment; they protect it by reducing unnecessary noise\n- Tools can accelerate production, but leadership systems determine whether scale strengthens impact or simply increases activity\n- High-impact marketing depends on leadership systems designed to protect effectiveness at scale\n---\n### [2026-05-15] [Tier A] A advocacia pública em busca do ‘melhor dos mundos’ entre Estado e mercado\n**Source:** https://www.jota.info/opiniao-e-analise/artigos/a-advocacia-publica-em-busca-do-melhor-dos-mundos-entre-estado-e-mercado\n**Key Insights:** - A AGU é uma instituição do Poder Executivo subordinada à chefia de governo, não um poder independente como o Judiciário ou Ministério Público\n- A organização da AGU depende de lei complementar e não cabe uma PEC que a equipare ao Judiciário ou ao Ministério Público\n- Nenhum órgão da administração pública pode se blindar do controle democrático e da hierarquia constitucional\n- Carreiras jurídicas de elite têm influenciado o processo legislativo e decisões orçamentárias que moldam as regras de sua própria atuação\n- A PEC 17/2024 prevê o repasse de duodécimos à AGU, retirando da chefia do Executivo a capacidade de alocar recursos segundo prioridades públicas\n- A estabilidade do regime estatutário já garante aos membros da AGU autonomia técnica para atuar sem interferências indevidas\n- A Lei Complementar 73/1993 já proíbe expressamente que membros da AGU exerçam advocacia privada\n- Revogação da proibição de advocacia privada por lei ordinária violaria o art. 131 da Constituição\n- Membros da AGU detêm poder decisório sobre interesses de terceiros e acesso a informações sigilosas do Estado\n- Permitir advocacia privada criaria conflito de interesses estrutural e vantagens competitivas desiguais no mercado jurídico\n- Honorários de sucumbência para advogados públicos são uma prática raramente encontrada em países da OCDE\n- Honorários de sucumbência funcionam como vetor de ampliação de rendimentos, tensionando o teto constitucional\n- A concentração de poder e privilégios produz pressão orçamentária, distorções na gestão de pessoas e desigualdade entre carreiras\n---\n### [2026-05-15] [Tier A] Entre a Lei da Dosimetria e a Representação 253/SC\n**Source:** https://www.jota.info/opiniao-e-analise/artigos/entre-a-lei-da-dosimetria-e-a-representacao-253-sc\n**Key Insights:** - A Mesa Diretora do Congresso Nacional declarou a prejudicialidade de parcela dos dispositivos vetados do Veto nº 3/2026, resultando no desmembramento da apreciação parlamentar e na promulgação da Lei 15.402/2026 contendo apenas disposições remanescentes\n- A principal contestação ao procedimento adotado sustentava que o veto total seria ato incindível, não podendo ser decomposto pelo Parlamento, e sua rejeição parcial transformaria indevidamente veto total em sucessão de vetos parciais autônomos\n- A Constituição brasileira não contém disposição explícita sobre se o Congresso pode rejeitar apenas parcela do veto presidencial\n- Em 1954, o governador de Santa Catarina Irineu Bornhausen vetou totalmente o Projeto de Lei nº 1.136 porque considerou que vetar apenas artigos específicos deixaria o documento sem harmonia e nexo, apesar de originalmente pretender veto parcial\n- O STF, na Representação nº 253/SC de 1956, decidiu unanimemente que é legítima a rejeição parcial de veto total pelo Poder Legislativo, baseando-se no princípio de simetria entre Executivo e Legislativo\n- A fundamentação do STF amparou-se na doutrina de Themístocles Brandão Cavalcanti, segundo a qual o Congresso recebe o exame pleno da lei enriquecido com as razões do Executivo, podendo reconhecer a procedência do veto apenas em alguns preceitos\n- O poder de desmembramento do veto pelo Legislativo possui limites materiais, devendo observar os parâmetros do art. 66, § 2º da Constituição, limitando-se a texto integral de artigo, parágrafo, inciso ou alínea\n- O desmembramento do veto é instrumento que permite avaliação mais detida das razões do Executivo, levando a sério a motivação apresentada ao autorizar parlamentares avaliarem sua pertinência em face de cada disposição\n- Divergências políticas sobre o procedimento adotado pelo Congresso não se confundem com juízo de inconstitucionalidade, sendo esta distinção uma exigência de rigor analítico e maturidade institucional\n---\n### [2026-05-15] [Tier A] Contas vinculadas no TCU: a tese que pode destravar a EF-118 e a nova política ferroviária\n**Source:** https://www.jota.info/opiniao-e-analise/colunas/infra/contas-vinculadas-no-tcu-a-tese-que-pode-destravar-a-ef-118-e-a-nova-politica-ferroviaria\n**Key Insights:** - A EF-118 é o primeiro leilão ferroviário previsto no cronograma de 2026, com investimentos de R$ 6,6 bilhões e capacidade de 24 milhões de toneladas por ano\n- O modelo de financiamento da EF-118 concentra aproximadamente R$ 4,1 bilhões em investimentos cruzados de três empresas ferroviárias depositados em conta vinculada\n- A ANTT manifestou preocupação quanto à bancabilidade e viabilidade econômico-financeira do projeto, que apresentou VPL negativo nos estudos iniciais\n- O TCU está analisando em tese a legalidade e limites do uso de contas vinculadas em processos de desestatização através da Representação TC 008.723/2023-0\n- As contas vinculadas representam estrutura jurídica onde recursos ficam segregados do caixa das partes e são movimentados conforme regras contratuais rígidas\n- O instrumento de contas vinculadas tem sido empregado no setor de concessões federais desde 2021, começando com a 4ª etapa de concessões rodoviárias\n- O TCU adotou postura restritiva em 2023, determinando que recursos de outorga fossem recolhidos à Conta Única do Tesouro nos casos dos Portos de São Sebastião e Itajaí\n- O Acórdão 2186/2025 do TCU autorizou por unanimidade o uso de conta vinculada para R$ 2,8 bilhões no contexto da renovação da Malha Regional Sudeste da MRS\n- A carteira ferroviária 2026/2027 prevê oito leilões com investimentos totais de R$ 140 bilhões que dependem da validação do instrumento de contas vinculadas\n- O uso de contas vinculadas permite que recursos decorrentes de concessões maduras financiem novos projetos sem que a União abra mão da destinação pública dos recursos\n- O processo da EF-118 no TCU (024.363/2025-1) está em fase de instrução com expectativa de julgamento no primeiro semestre de 2026\n- A Unidade de Auditoria Especializada em Orçamento do TCU (AudFiscal) enxerga no modelo de contas vinculadas um risco de bypass da regra de unidade do caixa da União\n---\n### [2026-05-15] [Tier A] Figma Beats, Raises and Accelerates! Boom! Stock Rockets 12%! But … It Still Trades for Less than 10X ARR\n**Source:** https://www.saastr.com/figma-beats-raises-and-accelerates-boom-stock-rockets-12-but-it-still-trades-for-less-than-10x-arr/\n**Key Insights:** - Figma's revenue grew 46% year-over-year in Q1 2026, beating analyst estimates by $17.1 million\n- Figma demonstrated accelerating growth for two consecutive quarters, with growth rates increasing from 38% to 40% to 46%\n- Net dollar retention reached 139%, the highest level in over two years\n- Figma's paid customer base grew 54% year-over-year to approximately 690,000\n- AI tools are driving upgrades rather than seat compression, with Pro Team conversions up 150% YoY\n- Enterprise customers ($100K+ ARR) grew 48% year-over-year, showing accelerating enterprise traction\n- Over 75% of enterprise users who exceeded their AI credit limits continued consuming credits in April, validating the monetization model\n- Figma launched AI credit monetization on March 18, contributing less than two weeks to Q1 results\n- Gross margin dipped to 82% due to AI inference costs, but remains strong for a hybrid AI-consumption business\n- Figma raised full-year 2026 revenue guidance by $55 million to $1.422-$1.428 billion, implying 35% growth at midpoint\n- Operating income guidance increased 25%+ from $100-110M to $125-135M for fiscal year 2026\n- Figma achieved a Rule of 73 quarter with 46% growth and 27% free cash flow margin\n- Despite strong performance, Figma trades at less than 10x ARR with a market cap of $10-11B and $1.33B implied ARR\n- Figma's stock is down 46% year-to-date and about 40% from IPO price despite strong Q1 results\n- Public software multiples have dramatically compressed from 2021 levels, when companies with this profile would have traded at 30-40x ARR\n- Companies that were expected to be disrupted by AI are becoming the biggest beneficiaries of AI adoption\n- AI expands deep B2B workflow products rather than replacing them, making seats more valuable\n- Consumption-based AI monetization layered on seat-based SaaS creates a successful hybrid model\n---\n### [2026-05-08] [Tier S] Melhor CRM B2B BR (Elas no Brasil)\n**Source:** https://elas.nobrasil.com.br/melhor-crm-b2b/\n**Key Insights:** - RD vs HubSpot vs Pipedrive análise BR.\n⚠️ Pre-2026-05-12 entry — verify independently before citing.\n---\n### [2026-05-08] [Tier S] State of Direct Response Copywriting 2026 (Rob Palmer)\n**Source:** https://robpalmer.com/blog/state-of-direct-response-copywriting-2026\n**Key Insights:** - Industry split: AI-commodity vs strategic persuasion architecture.\n⚠️ Pre-2026-05-12 entry — verify independently before citing.\n---\n### [2026-05-08] [Tier S] Como vender high-ticket — Funil (Conrado Adolpho)\n**Source:** https://conrado.com.br/como-vender-servicos-caros-high-ticket/\n**Key Insights:** - Funil high-ticket BR Conrado.\n⚠️ Pre-2026-05-12 entry — verify independently before citing.\n---\n### [2026-05-08] [Tier S] Conrado Adolpho — site oficial\n**Source:** https://conrado.com.br/\n**Key Insights:** - 8Ps Marketing Digital. 9 Públicos + Sistema MCC.\n⚠️ Pre-2026-05-12 entry — verify independently before citing.\n---\n### [2026-05-08] [Tier S] Erico Rocha — Fórmula de Lançamento site oficial\n**Source:** https://www.ericorocha.com.br/\n**Key Insights:** - FL: 6 dígitos em 7 dias. 40k+ alunos. Base Jeff Walker PLF.\n⚠️ Pre-2026-05-12 entry — verify independently before citing.\n---\n### [2026-05-08] [Tier S] $100M Leads Goodreads\n**Source:** https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/196239284-100m-leads\n**Key Insights:** - Goodreads page.\n⚠️ Pre-2026-05-12 entry — verify independently before citing.\n---\n### [2026-05-08] [Tier S] $100M Leads — Hormozi (Acquisition.com Shop)\n**Source:** https://shop.acquisition.com/products/single-hardback\n**Key Insights:** - $100M Lea